;; goi's divergences from gc at v1 (doc/go/GOI-SPEC.md, "v1's divergences (2026-10-20)", GR10): the
;; classes every program of bin/goi check that does not pass falls into, each with why it is by
;; design or deferred and where that was decided. A program's class is the first whose :match
;; finds its result and reason ("RESULT REASON", as the references and test/goi/check-known.edn
;; write them). bin/goi divergences checks the references against them (test/goi/divergences.ae).
;; Since 2026-10-24 (GOI-SPEC.md "As built: GC157 (b) and GS14 (a)") no class is deferred: the two
;; deferred at v1 (go:embed; byte, rune and aliases named by the types they denote) are built.
;; Since 2026-11-22 (GOI-SPEC.md "Since v1: gc's -std, -+, -complete and -p, ...") four classes are
;; empty and gone: :call-depth (peano, program mode's depth limit, queue 426), :std-weak-unique
;; (fixedbugs/issue68415, unique importable), :std-out-of-scope (escape_runtime_atomic, internal std
;; packages from std's forms in errorcheck) and :spellings (fixedbugs/bug217, the extra receivers
;; dropped as gc's syntax drops them).
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :foreign-code
  :title "assembly, cgo, go:linkname"
  :kind :design
  :why "goi interprets Go forms; a function written in assembly (or bodiless), cgo and go:linkname's pulls of gc's symbols have no forms to interpret (a bodiless function in a package without assembly is refused at its first call since 2026-11-19, queue 420: gc links it only where no live call reaches it, fixedbugs/issue9608.go)"
  :decided "§1.1"
  :match [#"^unsupported assembly \(" #"^unsupported go:linkname \(" #"^unsupported a function without a body \(assembly\)" #"^unsupported .*cgo"]}
 {:id :package-tests
  :title "package tests"
  :kind :design
  :why "goi loads a package's own files, not its _test.go files (:test-files); no program of the check needs them"
  :decided "§1.1, S45"
  :match [#"^unsupported .*(:test-files|_test\.go)"]}
 {:id :memory
  :title "finalizer timing, escape analysis, memory statistics, heap profiles"
  :kind :design
  :why "the collector sees the interpreter's frames, closures and allocations, not gc's escape analysis and stack allocation (dead slots are cleared since 2026-11-05, so a finalizer's timing follows gc's liveness; what is left holds a value in goi's own registries, or is the allocation profile)"
  :decided "§1.1"
  :match [#"^known .*(finalizer|escape analysis|ReadMemStats|heap profile|AllocsPerRun|uintptrescapes|liveness of stack objects)"]}
 {:id :unsafe-layout
  :title "unsafe layout and memory order gc decides"
  :kind :design
  :why "addresses of the data segment and the order of gc's generated comparisons over memory protected by the program are gc's code generation"
  :decided "§1.1, §5.4"
  :match [#"^known unsafe addresses" #"^known == of interfaces holding structs"]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: programs over the check's time budget"
  :kind :budget
  :why "a failure of the check's budget, not by design (GOI-DESIGN-REVIEW.md, Proposed 3 (b), decided 2026-11-05): an interpreter is 10-100 times slower than gc's code, and the budget is a program's limit in test/goi/timeouts.txt (the check's default 10 s); a program leaves the class when its budget there lets it pass"
  :decided "§11.1, GR3's criterion; GOI-DESIGN-REVIEW.md Proposed 3 (b)"
  :match [#"^known speed: "]}
 {:id :gc-m
  :title "gc's -m of other packages' generic instances"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "since 2026-11-06 gc's -m is goi's port of gc's escape analysis and inliner (GOI-SPEC.md \"Since v1: gc's escape analysis and inliner\"), since 2026-11-17 with the package's own generic functions' and types' instances stenciled as gc's noder does (\"Since v1: gc's -m of generic instances\"); what it does not do yet: the instances of another package's generic functions and types, which gc stencils in the importing package (escape_unique.go: unique.Make[T], unique.Handle[T])"
  :decided "GOI-SPEC.md \"Decided (2026-11-06, the user: ...)\": Proposed 1 (a), with goi's next round of generics; \"Since v1: gc's -m of generic instances\", Proposed 1 (taken overnight, round 52: kept deferred)"
  :match [#"^known gc's -m: "]}
 {:id :gc-flags
  :title "gc's optimizer diagnostics and flags"
  :kind :design
  :why "liveness, the write barriers, the SSA back end's passes and their debug output (-live, -l=N, -wb, -d=...): gc's phases after type checking, which goi does not have (gc's -m with or without -l, -N, -smallframes, -d=escapemutationscalls, zerocopy and inlfuncswithclosures are goi's port since 2026-11-06: GOI-SPEC.md \"Since v1: gc's escape analysis and inliner\"; -d=typeassert, defer, append, slice and checkptr's inliner refusals since 2026-11-19, queue 420: \"Since v1: gc's front-end -d diagnostics\"; -d=escapedebug's dataWord since 2026-11-22); and the run programs built with -gcflags whose output is what the flag makes gc's code do (run since 2026-11-04, gc's reference built with the action's flags: GOI-SPEC.md \"Since v1: gc's flags of run actions\")"
  :decided "§1.1, GC46"
  :match [#"^unsupported -(m|l|live|N|wb|smallframes)(=[^:]*)?: " #"^unsupported -d=[^:]*: " #"^skip the action needs gc flags: " #"^known gc flags: "]}
 {:id :gc-std
  :title "gc compiling std or the runtime"
  :kind :design
  :why "-std, -+, -complete, -asmhdr, -spectre: gc's modes for compiling the standard library and the runtime; since 2026-11-22 -std, -+, -complete and -p are goi's (noder's pragma checks, writer's missing function body, the escape analysis' and walk's runtime errors, the inliner's GetCallerPC: GOI-SPEC.md \"Since v1: gc's -std, -+, -complete and -p, ...\"); what is left: gc's write barrier checks under -+ (go:nowritebarrier, nowritebarrier.go: ssa/writebarrier.go's needwb over the SSA values and ssagen/nowb.go's call graph after inlining, gc's back end)"
  :decided "§1.1, GC46"
  :match [#"^unsupported -(std|\+|complete|asmhdr|spectre)[^:]*: "]}
 {:id :gc-phases
  :title "errors of gc's phases after type checking"
  :kind :design
  :why "go/types reports none of the expected errors: they are gc's SSA back end's (a stack frame too large: the frame gc's back end lays out), which goi does not have; noder's pragma checks are gc's front end's, judged since GPS41 (c), and its types' sizes (a channel's or a map's element too large, an array beyond the address space) since 2026-11-04 (GOI-SPEC.md \"Since v1: gc's size checks\")"
  :decided "GC46, GPS41 (c)"
  :match [#"^unsupported errors of gc's phases after type checking"]}
 {:id :gc-reference
  :title "gc's own errors no longer pass the test"
  :kind :na
  :why "go1.27.1's gc fails the program's own // ERROR comments (its messages changed since the test was written): there is no reference to judge goi against"
  :decided "DECISION B (a) (round 51, the user, 2026-11-17): no reference, so not applicable (not in the denominator), as divergences-aot.edn's :no-forms; GR7b"
  :match [#"^skip gc's own errorcheck does not pass here"]}
 {:id :gc-run
  :title "gc's own run no longer passes the test"
  :kind :design
  :why "go1.27.1's gc's run of the original does not pass Go's test driver here (a status not 0, or output other than the golden .out): there is no reference to judge goi against"
  :decided "queue 011 (report 002, finding 5)"
  :match [#"^skip gc's own run does not pass here"]}
 {:id :arch-constraint
  :title "a program of another architecture"
  :kind :design
  :why "gc's reference is linux/amd64's; a program whose build constraint is amd64 has no Go files for tamago/arm64"
  :decided "the arm64 box check"
  :match [#"^known its build constraint is amd64"]}
 {:id :box-console
  :title "the box's console"
  :kind :design
  :why "in the box, TamaGo's console is one stream and the board's line buffer ends an unterminated last line with a newline"
  :decided "GC35, GR7a"
  :match [#"^known the box's console"]}
]
